  Digital memoryless (or static) symbol time predistortion                                                            0                                    0
is a method for reducing the undesired eﬀects of nonlinear
ampliﬁcation. Since it considers only the current symbol,                                                             -1                                   -1
it does not compensate for clustering (due to the mem-
ory eﬀect) but only for warping. On the other hand, it has                                                            -2                                   -2
signiﬁcantly lower computational complexity with respect                                                              -2 -1 0 1 2                          -2 -1 0 1 2
to methods with memory, or dynamic; the latter, in fact,
are commonly based on the solution of M2Q+1 equations,                                                                       In-Phase                          In-Phase
so that their complexity increases exponentially with the
memory Q of the predistortion process.                                                                    Figure 10 APSK constellation with predistortion.

